Z","assignee":{"login":"katre","id":326527,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNjUyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/326527?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre","html_url":"https://github.com/katre","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/814256915","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/13301#issuecomment-814256915","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/13301","id":814256915,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDgxNDI1NjkxNQ==","user":{"login":"katre","id":326527,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNjUyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/326527?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre","html_url":"https://github.com/katre","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-04-06T16:26:41Z","updated_at":"2021-04-06T16:26:41Z","body":"Debugging this is interesting. The failure occurs in [`RecursivePackageProviderBackedTargetPatternResolver.findTargetsBeneathDirectory`](https://cs.opensource.google/bazel/bazel/+/master:src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/skyframe/RecursivePackageProviderBackedTargetPatternResolver.java;bpv=1;bpt=1;l=178?ss=bazel&q=RecursivePackageProviderBackedTargetPatternResolver&gsn=findTargetsBeneathDirectory&gs=kythe%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fbazelbuild%2Fbazel%3Flang%3Djava%3Fpath%3Dcom.google.devtools.build.lib.skyframe.RecursivePackageProviderBackedTargetPatternResolver%23a74a8014e625dc96f001920591148c4c7e9526db4784cf34db9b9ecdbd9fa764&gs=kythe%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fbazelbuild%2Fbazel%3Flang%3Djava%3Fpath%3Dcom.google.devtools.build.lib.skyframe.RecursivePackageProviderBackedTargetPatternResolver%23c4ef40ece663721c3715e97b161d0adbdd5f67636a1882f3a78103de25467dc7).\r\n\r\nThe first time this is called, the `RecursivePackageProvider` is a [`EnvironmentBackedRecursivePackageProvider`](https://cs.opensource.google/bazel/bazel/+/master:src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/skyframe/EnvironmentBackedRecursivePackageProvider.java;bpv=1;bpt=1;l=52?ss=bazel&q=EnvironmentBackedRecursivePackageProvider&gsn=EnvironmentBackedRecursivePackageProvider&gs=kythe%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fbazelbuild%2Fbazel%3Flang%3Djava%3Fpath%3Dcom.google.devtools.build.lib.skyframe.EnvironmentBackedRecursivePackageProvider%231ec19537684f3ce33145ea2a95cb9aa1988b01225db6d50fba3a4759066c2423), and this correctly returns the targets.\r\n\r\nThe second time, however, the `RecursivePackageProvider` is a [`GraphBackedRecursivePackageProvider`](https://cs.opensource.google/bazel/bazel/+/master:src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/skyframe/GraphBackedRecursivePackageProvider.java;bpv=1;bpt=1;l=56?ss=bazel&q=GraphBackedRecursivePackageProvider&gsn=GraphBackedRecursivePackageProvider&gs=kythe%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fbazelbuild%2Fbazel%3Flang%3Djava%3Fpath%3Dcom.google.devtools.build.lib.skyframe.GraphBackedRecursivePackageProvider%23536f1dd5dba9e42e1fad48d9ea619ee9393d64d753f3f8cf5b544a9a5cb86274), which returns no targets. This appears to be because this implementation is checking the `universeTargetPatterns`, and that is set to `//...`, which does not match `@remotejdk11_linux`, and so all targets are filtered out.\r\n\r\nSo the question is: why are there multiple instances of `RecursivePackageProviderBackedTargetPatternResolver` in use, why are they different, and is this the correct use of `universeTargetPatterns`?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/814256915/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"katre","id":326527,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNjUyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/326527?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre","html_url":"https://github.com/katre","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/814304288","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/13301#issuecomment-814304288","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/13301","id":814304288,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDgxNDMwNDI4OA==","user":{"login":"katre","id":326527,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNjUyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/326527?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre","html_url":"https://github.com/katre","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-04-06T17:36:41Z","updated_at":"2021-04-06T17:36:41Z","body":"It looks like that universe scope is defined from the [`PostAnalysisQueryEnvironment`](https://cs.opensource.google/bazel/bazel/+/master:src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/query2/PostAnalysisQueryEnvironment.java;l=110). However, the code is clearly wrong: `//...` does not mean \"all patterns\", it means \"all patterns in the main repository\". I'm going to investigate if this can be fixed.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, this ignores the `--universe_scope` flag.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/814304288/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"katre","i